# Hexplain Aspect — Time (hx-time) 1.0
# Orthogonal aspect: temporal extent and structure of data.
# Imports nothing; imported by any domain whose data has a timeline (audio, video, animation).
@prefix :       <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/time#> .
@prefix atime:  <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/time#> .
@prefix owl:    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:    <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix skos:   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix ma:     <http://www.w3.org/ns/ma-ont#> .
@prefix qudt:   <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .
@prefix quantitykind: <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/> .
@prefix unit:   <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix dcterms:<http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix vann:   <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/> .

<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/time> a owl:Ontology ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/time/1.0> ; owl:versionInfo "1.0" ;
    rdfs:label "Hexplain Aspect — Time (hx-time)" ;
    rdfs:comment "Orthogonal aspect for the temporal extent and structure of data (duration, and — as the aspect grows — timebase, frame count, timecode). Imported by any domain whose data has a timeline." ;
    dcterms:created "2026-07-22"^^xsd:date ; dcterms:creator <https://geoknoesis.com> ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "atime" ; vann:preferredNamespaceUri "https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/time#" .

:duration a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "duration" ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/time> ; rdfs:seeAlso ma:duration ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ; qudt:hasQuantityKind quantitykind:Time ; qudt:hasUnit unit:SEC ; rdfs:comment "Playing time in seconds." .

@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
:DurationShape a sh:NodeShape ; sh:targetSubjectsOf :duration ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :duration ; sh:or ( [ sh:datatype xsd:decimal ] [ sh:datatype xsd:integer ] ) ; sh:minInclusive 0 ; sh:maxCount 1 ] .

# BEGIN GENERATED TERM DOCUMENTATION
# Editorial annotations only; OWL axioms and SHACL constraints above are unchanged.
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/time> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Orthogonal aspect for the temporal extent and structure of data (duration, and — as the aspect grows — timebase, frame count, timecode). Imported by any domain whose data has a timeline."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/time> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for temporal metadata of content. Numeric durations and frame/sample counts are not interchangeable without a timing model."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/time#DurationShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for atime:duration. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/time#DurationShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using atime:duration Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/time#DurationShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Duration Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/time#DurationShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/time> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/time#duration> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The elapsed playing time of content expressed in seconds. It is a temporal extent, distinct from a timestamp or a count of frames or samples."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/time#duration> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for temporal metadata of content. Numeric durations and frame/sample counts are not interchangeable without a timing model. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
